NEO GEO ARTBOX SDK - GRAPHICS PIPELINE
========================================

The Artbox pipeline converts PNG images into Neo Geo compatible sprite and FIX tile formats.

CORE TOOLS
----------
img2neo.py
    Primary image processor. Maps PNG colours to the Neo Geo 4096-colour palette.
    Supports k-means clustering for optimal 15-colour palette generation.
    Implements Floyd-Steinberg dithering to preserve detail within the 16-colour limit.

romtiles.py
    Tile encoder and ROM packer. Slices processed images into 16x16 sprite tiles
    (C ROMs) or 8x8 FIX tiles (S ROM) and generates the corresponding ROM files.

fixtiles.py
    S1 (FIX) ROM builder. Generates the 128 KB 777-s1.s1 from three sources:
      1. sfix.sfix system ROM - standard NeoGeo font area.
      2. Existing 777-s1.s1 - non-infix base font tiles preserved.
      3. infix/*.png images - custom tiles written deterministically
                              starting at tile position 256.
    Outputs 777-s1.s1 in hardware format directly (no post-processing required).

createromdb.py
    Initialises the neorom.db SQLite database (image and imagefix tables).

romdbimgimport.py
    Imports sprite source images from in/ into the image DB table.

romdbfiximport.py
    Imports all indexed-palette PNGs from infix/ into the imagefix DB table.
    Auto-detects all images (no hardcoded count limit).

genmapdb.py / genscreens.py
    Generate tile maps and screen layout data from source images.

DIRECTORY STRUCTURE
-------------------
artbox/in/      - Sprite source PNGs (16x16 tile multiples recommended).
artbox/infix/   - FIX layer source PNGs (8x8 multiples, indexed palette, max 15 colours).
artbox/map/     - Tile mapping data.

USAGE
-----
1. Place sprite images in in/ and FIX images in infix/.
2. Run:  make art    (rebuild C ROMs from sprites)
          make sfix   (rebuild S1 FIX ROM from infix images)
          make srom   (alias for make sfix)
3. ROMs are written to roms/<game>/.

FIX LAYER IMAGE REQUIREMENTS
-----------------------------
  Format:  PNG, indexed palette (mode P in Pillow)
  Colours: maximum 15 (palette index 0 = transparent)
  Size:    multiple of 8 pixels in both dimensions
  Convert: GIMP Image > Mode > Indexed, max 15 colours, or
           Pillow: img.quantize(colors=15).save(path)

REQUIREMENTS
------------
  Python 3.8+, numpy, pypng, pysqlite3 (or sqlite3)

Dithering and Palette Generation
--------------------------------
img2neo.py automatically handles 24-bit to Neo Geo palette conversion.
k-means clustering preserves the most important colours; FS dithering blends
transitions to avoid harsh banding on the 16-colour limit.
